, 1, 2 and 3.\n\n2. **Central block.** A block of colour 4 is painted on top of the quadrants, inset 2 cells from every edge of the rectangle.\n   - 10×12 rectangle in pair 1: the 4-block is rows 3–8, cols 7–14.\n   - 8×12 rectangle in pair 1: the 4-block is rows 16–19, cols 3–10.\n   - 8×8 rectangle in pair 2: the 4-block is rows 3–6, cols 4–7.\n\n   The inset is 2 in every case. So only a 2-cell-wide ring of each quadrant colour stays visible around the centre.\n\nAll rectangles in the examples and the test have even width and height, so the quadrants are exact halves.\n\n**Applying it to the test**\n\nThe test has three rectangles:\n- 10×6 at rows 1–10, cols 3–8: quadrants are 5×3, and the 4-block is rows 3–8, cols 5–6.\n- 14×10 at rows 4–17, cols 12–21: quadrants are 7×5, and the 4-block is rows 6–15, cols 14–19.\n- 6×6 at rows 15–20, cols 3–8: quadrants are 3×3, and the 4-block is rows 17–18, cols 5–6.\n\n**Teaching stages**\n\nFor each rectangle the program records two stages:\n1. after painting the four quadrant colours;\n2. after painting the central 4-block.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        h, w = y1 - y0 + 1, x1 - x0 + 1\n        my, mx = y0 + h // 2, x0 + w // 2\n        out[y0:my, x0:mx] = 6\n        out[y0:my, mx:x1 + 1] = 1\n        out[my:y1 + 1, x0:mx] = 2\n        out[my:y1 + 1, mx:x1 + 1] = 3\n        emit(out, f\"Split rectangle at ({y0},{x0})-({y1},{x1}) into quadrants 6/1/2/3.\")\n        out[y0 + 2:y1 - 1, x0 + 2:x1 - 1] = 4\n        emit(out, f\"Paint the central block (inset 2) of that rectangle with 4.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each 8-coloured rectangle is recoloured in place; no cell outside a rectangle changes."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Central block.** A block of colour 4 is painted on top of the quadrants, inset 2 cells from every edge of the rectangle."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"5229a0b8b8b015ec0323f7f27ce85aec637bd131c4e3d87154af832cb0c6805d","task_sha256":"03b598bbd4d2676ecfff0211420cc40b41852ed9095dbbf3ac2250ee448b1bc9","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
